{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Counting problems can be approached from the basic building blocks described in the first section: ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "class": null,
        "href": "https://{{pathToRoot}}/counting",
        "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
        "target": "_blank"
       },
       "type": "link"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Counting",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": ". However some counting problems are so ubiquitous in the world of probability that it is worth knowing a few higher level counting abstractions. When solving problems, if you can find the analogy from these canonical examples you can build off of the corresponding combinatorics formulas:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "start": "1"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
       },
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [
          {
           "attrs": {
            "class": null,
            "href": "https://#perm_distinct",
            "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
            "target": "_blank"
           },
           "type": "link"
          }
         ],
         "text": "Permutations of Distinct Objects",
         "type": "text"
        }
       ],
       "type": "paragraph"
      }
     ],
     "type": "listItem"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
       },
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [
          {
           "attrs": {
